    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0333" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/767: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="26" xml:id="d359-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-13T17:30:00+08:00">September 13, 1937—5:30
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 13—1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0013. To enable largest possible number nationals to evacuate China ports via <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Canopus, Chaumont</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Gold
                        Star</hi> all officers’ dependents proceeding United States will be left in
                    northern ports, <hi rendition="#italic">Canopus</hi> will return to northern
                    ports via Hong Kong and Woosung, then proceed Kobe with these dependents
                    proceeding United States commercially. <hi rendition="#italic">Canopus</hi> will
                    then return Manila via China ports evacuating nationals as necessary.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
